# Exceptions to the Trivy gates (image-scan and fs-scan). Trivy reads this file automatically
# from the repository root.
#
# The gate fails the build on a FIXABLE HIGH or CRITICAL vulnerability. The right answer is almost
# always to fix it: bump the dependency or the base image (Dependabot opens those pull requests).
# An exception is for the rare case where that is impossible for now (no fixed base image exists
# yet) and the vulnerable code cannot be reached. Rules, all mandatory:
#
#   1. One line per CVE, with a comment ABOVE it that says: why it does not apply or cannot be
#      fixed yet, who decided, and the date.
#   2. Every line ends with  exp:YYYY-MM-DD  (at most 90 days ahead). Trivy stops honouring an
#      entry on that date, the finding comes back and the build fails again: an exception can
#      never be forgotten.
#   3. Never ignore a whole package or a whole image; only specific CVE ids.
#   4. Remove the line as soon as the fix is available.
#
# Example (NOT active, this is a comment):
#   # CVE-2099-0001: only reachable through the XML parser, which we do not use. Decided
#   # 2026-11-07 by <name>; no fixed base image published yet.
#   CVE-2099-0001 exp:2027-01-15
#
# Currently no exceptions: every finding so far was fixed instead (see D54, D74).
